        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: へんこうする",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "へんこうする — henkō suru — \"to change a plan; to alter (a date)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "もし あめが ふったら、よていを へんこうします。 — moshi ame ga futtara, yotei o henkō shimasu — \"If it rains, we will change the plan.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Polite へんこうします, henkōshimasu; a する verb. Past (polite): かいしゃが よていを へんこうしました。, kaisha ga yotei o henkō shimashita."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "へんこうする (henkō suru) is built from a Sino-Japanese noun and the native verb suru, \"to do\". The noun, henkō, is two Chinese characters read with their on'yomi, readings borrowed from Chinese: hen, \"change\" (Middle Chinese pjenH) and kō, \"renew\" (kaeng) (KANJIDIC2; JMdict; Middle Chinese in Baxter's transcription)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
